# I1 of the dilla-media task-9 review, (3a): any committed Remove of a leaf satisfies the instance's
# outstanding Remove of that leaf (protocol/02 invariant 4 clause 1).
#
# carol posts her own Remove, then is kicked: the instance issues its Remove on top of hers. alice's
# queue holds carol's Remove BEHIND the instance's (`member_removes_last`), the order a committer
# not built on dilla-core may hold, so OpenMLS commits carol's Remove and leaves the instance's
# unreferenced. Before the fix clause 1 refused that commit with outstanding_proposals until the
# TTL, and charged the committer a lost round each time. Now it is accepted: carol's leaf is gone,
# the instance's row is deleted with the commit, and nothing is re-issued at the new epoch. The Go
# test that runs this reads the instance afterwards.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group call kind=call target=e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6 community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
leave carol call
kick alice carol
expect_425 send alice call the kick is issued over carol's own remove
sync alice
commit alice call member_removes_last
sync bob
kick alice carol
send alice call carol is out
expect_decrypts bob call carol is out
